course: dictionary
lesson: 14073
title: The big word maximisation
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Maximisation is a long word, but its parts help. Maximise means to make something as big, high or great as possible. The ending -ation turns the action into a thing, so maximisation is the act of doing that.
explain: «The shop worked on the maximisation of sales by putting its best toys by the door.» The shop wanted to sell as many toys as it could. The words sales and best toys are clues: the goal is to make sales as big as possible.
explain: Maths uses the word in a special way. «In the maths lesson, the task was maximisation: find the largest area a fence of 20 metres can enclose.» Words like area and largest tell you it means finding the biggest possible value. Its opposite is minimisation, making something as small as possible.
fact: Maximisation means making something as big, high or great as possible.
fact: In maths, maximisation means finding the largest possible value of something under some rules.
fact: With 20 m of fence, a square of 5 m by 5 m gives the largest area: 25 m².
fact: «Profit maximisation» means trying to earn as much money as possible.
fact: The opposite of maximisation is minimisation. In US spelling, the word is «maximization».
exercise: «The farmer wanted the maximisation of his crop.» What does maximisation mean here? | Selling the farm | Watering the field once a year | *Making the crop as big as possible | Cutting the crop down to a few plants
exercise: Maths problem: What is the largest area of a square field you can fence with 20 m of fence? | 9 m² | 36 m² | 16 m² | *25 m²
exercise: Which word is the opposite of maximisation? | *Minimisation | Sensation | Multiplication | Celebration
test: «The company focused on profit maximisation, trying to earn as much money as it could.» What does profit maximisation mean? | Spending less on paper | Counting money every hour | Giving money away | *Earning as much money as possible
test: Which is the best meaning of maximisation in maths? | Adding two numbers together | *Finding the largest possible value under some rules | Finding the smallest value | Drawing a shape
exam: «A scientist aimed for the maximisation of energy from her solar panel.» What was her goal? | To paint the panel blue | To turn the panel off | *To get as much energy as possible from the panel | To make the panel as small as possible
